<title>FRANCE: Two big Carrefour blocks traded.</title>
<headline>Two big Carrefour blocks traded.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two blocks of Carrefour shares were traded after-hours on Thursday following the retail group's annual general meeting, brokers said on Friday.</p>
<p>They said two blocks, of 257,000 Carrefour shares each, were traded at 3,405 francs per share and 3,403 francs respectively.</p>
<p>Carrefour chairman Daniel Bernard forecast a 15 to 20 percent profit rise for 1997 and a 10 percent sales rise at the AGM.</p>
<p>The stock was up 1.35 percent at 3,445 francs at 1035 GMT, in a slightly weaker market.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
